m/users/nmittler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nmittler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nmittler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nmittler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nmittler/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nmittler/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-04-17T13:28:22Z","updated_at":"2015-04-17T13:28:22Z","body":"IIUC, [this is the problem](https://github.com/netty/netty/blob/master/codec-http2/src/main/java/io/netty/handler/codec/http2/DefaultHttp2ConnectionDecoder.java#L268).  We just blindly try to create the stream without first checking if it's for a previously existing stream (by checking the streamId).  I think this should be easy to fix.  I'll try to throw together a PR.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/issues/comments/93985930/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"nmittler","id":6493296,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0OTMyOTY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6493296?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nmittler","html_url":"https://github.com/nmittler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nmittler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nmittler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nmittler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nmittler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nmittler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nmittler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nmittler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nmittler/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nmittler/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/issues/comments/94025599","html_url":"https://github.com/netty/netty/issues/3643#issuecomment-94025599","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/issues/3643","id":94025599,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDk0MDI1NTk5","user":{"login":"louiscryan","id":9046588,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNDY1ODg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9046588?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/louiscryan","html_url":"https://github.com/louiscryan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/louiscryan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/louiscryan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/louiscryan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/louiscryan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/louiscryan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/louiscryan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/louiscryan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/louiscryan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/louiscryan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-04-17T16:50:03Z","updated_at":"2015-04-17T16:50:03Z","body":"I see the same issue manifest in a different way.\n\nClients can send WINDOW_UPDATE to a server that has already closed it's stream. This occurs when the server sends a sequence of DATA frames and then immediately closes the stream. The client after processing some of the received DATA frames decides it needs to release more flow control and sends WINDOW_UPDATE.  This races with the server.\n\nThe client will happily process the other DATA frames but the server sees this as a fatal error and closes the connection which is ugly.\n","author_association":"NO